 "intent": "Map the PacBio HiFi/CCS reads of hifi_reads.fastq (read names look like movie/zmw/ccs) with STAR, keeping each read's complete original name in the alignment records, because the alignments will be joined by read name to the instrument's per-ZMW quality table.",
 "silent_error": "STAR cuts every read name at the first '/' by default (--readNameSeparator /, meant to drop /1 /2 mate suffixes). For PacBio names movie/zmw/ccs all 12 reads are written to Aligned.out.sam under the single name m64011_190830_220126, so the join with the per-ZMW table is impossible (or silently many-to-one). Mapping positions and flags are fine, there is no warning, and the parameter is documented in the STAR help (--readNameSeparator).",
